# TypeScript Standards

## Compiler

- `strict: true` in all `tsconfig.json` files
- No `any` — use `unknown` + type guards at boundaries
- Prefer `satisfies` over `as` for token objects

## Types

- `interface` for object shapes; `type` for unions/intersections
- Shared domain types in `packages/shared/` — never duplicate
- Branded types for `Square`, `Fen`, `San` where parsing matters

## API Boundaries

Validate external input with Zod at Express routes and Supabase edge functions:

```typescript
const DetectMotifsSchema = z.object({ fen: z.string().min(15) });
```

## Error Handling

```typescript
// ✅ Result type for expected failures
type Result<T, E> = { ok: true; value: T } | { ok: false; error: E };

// ✅ Structured API errors
{ error: string; code: string }
```

- Motif engine: `Result` — never throw for illegal FEN
- Voice pipeline: illegal moves are expected, not errors

## Imports

- Package-scoped aliases (`@mindboard/motif-engine`) — no deep relative paths across packages
- No circular deps between `chess-core` and `motif-engine`
